{
  "dom_id": "step-q319255",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na\u22a5b\\,\u27f9\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =3\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
